doc_list — implementation plan
==============================

status: done (2026-07-14)
"documentation for the agent (manuals, requirements, recap)".
wave 5 (documentation), pure scala — no MCP.ir, no ML.

the tool exposes the distribution's documentation CATALOG:
isabelle.Doc.contents() (Pure/Tools/doc.scala) parsed from
doc/Contents (+ release notes from ISABELLE_DOCS_RELEASE_NOTES,
examples from ISABELLE_DOCS_EXAMPLES), joined per entry to the
source session that generates it, so doc_read and search_sources
are reachable from the listing.

advertised metadata (the builtin table row)
-------------------------------------------

name          doc_list
description   "List the Isabelle documentation catalog: the manuals,
              release notes, and examples shipped with the
              distribution (what `isabelle doc` shows). Each entry
              reports name, title, its catalog section, and how it
              is readable: manuals name the source session whose
              theory files doc_read serves (chapter-level plain
