assumptions and how to test them
--------------------------------

(testing process: scala-unit cases in
mcp_test/src/mcp_handler_tests.scala, bridge cases in
mcp_test/src/mcp_bridge_tests.scala extending MCP_Session_Suite —
see plans/README "testing process". mcp_test runs inside the
isabelle environment, so the REAL Doc.contents() and session
structure of the bundled distribution are available to scala-unit
tests directly; no fake catalog needed for the join claims.)

T1  the join claim: every pdf manual in the bundled distribution
    resolves to a source session. assert at minimum the three
    naming shapes: "isar-ref" -> Isar_Ref (hyphen vs underscore),
    "logics-ZF" -> Logics_ZF (case + hyphen), "main" -> Main
    (name collision with the theory Main — the join is over doc
    sessions only, so no ambiguity).
    test [scala unit]: real Doc.contents() + real structure.
T2  variant parsing (D1, revised 2026-07-14 during implementation):
    Sessions.Structure already parses document_variants into
    List[Document_Build.Document_Variant] with .name stripped of any
    "=tags" suffix (Info.document_variants) -- no manual ":"/"="
    splitting needed, so this is no longer a claim about our own code.
    Retargeted at Doc_Catalog.join, the pure fold that maps every
    variant name to its session: a session with variant names
    ["a", "b"] (as "a:b=t" parses to) ends up with both "a" -> sess
    and "b" -> sess in the map.
    test [scala unit]: pure, over synthetic (session, variant-names)
    pairs -- no Sessions.Structure needed.
T3  plain entries: NEWS appears (release notes section) with a
    non-pdf path, rendered "plain", readable by doc_read.
    test [scala unit]: real catalog contains NEWS as plain.
T4  filtering is probe-safe: pattern "isar*" returns exactly the
    isar-ref entry; pattern "zzz*" returns an EMPTY listing with ok
    status, not an error.
    test [scala unit]: both.
T5  full chain: tools/list advertises the row above; tools/call
    doc_list over a live server returns a listing containing
    isar-ref with its source session named.
    test [bridge]: one MCP_Session_Suite case.

